# text = In a vast and golden saloon , that in its decorations would have become , and in its splendour would not have disgraced , Versailles in the days of the grand monarch , were assembled many whose hearts beat at the thought of the morrow , and whose brains still laboured to control its fortunes to their advantage lisped in a low voice a young man , lounging on the edge of a buhl table that had once belonged to a Mortemart , and dangling a rich cane with affected indifference in order to conceal his anxiety from all , except the person whom he addressed was the reply continued the gentleman with the cane , and with a look of uneasy superstition .
