# text = The old nobility of Spain delighted to address each other only by their names , when in the presence of a spick-and-span grandee ; calling each other Sidonia and then turning round with the most distinguished consideration , and appealing to the Most Noble Marquis of Ensenada said Lord de Mowbray said Lord Marney inquired Mr St Lys who was standing by said Mr St Lys said Lord Marney ; " they get more than that , because there is beer-money allowed , at least to a great extent among us , though I for one do not approve of the practice , and that makes nearly a shilling per week additional ; and then some of them have potatoe grounds , though I am entirely opposed to that system said Mr St Lys said Lord Marney said Mr St Lys ; " after his day's work if he returns to his own roof and finds no home : his fire extinguished , his food unprepared ; the partner of his life , wearied with labour in the field or the factory , still absent , or perhaps in bed from exhaustion , or because she has returned wet to the skin , and has no change of raiment for her relief .
