# text = At the beginning of the revolutionary war , Wodgate was a sort of squatting district of the great mining region to which it was contiguous , a place where adventurers in the industry which was rapidly developing , settled themselves ; for though the great veins of coal and ironstone cropped up , as they phrase it , before they reached this bare and barren land , and it was thus deficient in those mineral and metallic treasures which had enriched its neighbourhood , Wodgate had advantages of its own , and of a kind which touch the fancy of the lawless .
