# text = As Sybil and Egremont walked along , the race too tender for labour , seemed to spring out of every cottage to greet Her visits had been very rare of late , but they were never forgotten ; they formed epochs in the village annals of the children , some of whom knew only by tradition the golden age when Sybil Gerard lived at the great house , and daily glanced like a spirit among their homes , smiling and met with smiles , blessing and ever blessed she said to Egremont touching gently on his head a very serious urchin who had never left her side for a moment , proud of his position , and holding tight her hand with all his strength
