# text = Lady Joan was haughty and scientific , approved of much , but principally of the system of ventilation , of which she asked several questions which greatly perplexed Mrs Trafford , who slightly blushed , and looked at her husband for relief , but he was engaged with Lady Maud , who was full of enthusiasm , entered into everything with the zest of sympathy , identified herself with the factory system almost as much as she had done with the crusades , and longed to teach in singing schools , found public gardens , and bid fountains flow and sparkle for the people said Lord Milford , as he was cutting a pasty said Mr Mountchesney exclaimed Mrs Trafford asked Lady Maud said Mrs Trafford asked Lord Milford said Mr Trafford , addressing his answer to Lady Maud enquired Mr Mountchesney said Lady Maud she said , addressing herself to Lord de Mowbray said Lord de Mowbray with many smiles said Mr Trafford he added , with a smile and in a lower tone to Lady de Mowbray enquired her ladyship in a sugary tone said Mr Trafford said Lord Milford said Mr Trafford said Lord de Mowbray said Mr Trafford said Lady Joan to Mr Jermyn , who stared and bowed said Lady Firebrace to Mr Trafford , who smiled a negative enquired Lord de Mowbray said Mr Trafford said Lord de Mowbray looking a little confused said Mr Trafford said Lady Maud said Lord de Mowbray ; and then turning to Mrs Trafford he overwhelmed her with elaborate courtesies of phrase ; praised everything again ; first generally and then in detail ; the factory , which he seemed to prefer to his castle -- the house , which he seemed to prefer even to the factory -- the gardens , from which he anticipated even greater gratification than from the house .
