# text = Undeterred by her somewhat haughty demeanour , which Lady Maud only attributed to the novelty of her situation , her ignorance of the world , and her embarrassment under this overpowering condescension , the good-tempered and fussy daughter of Lord de Mowbray proceeded to re-assure Sybil , and to enforce on her that this perhaps unprecedented descent from superiority was not a mere transient courtliness of the moment , and that she really might rely on her patronage and favourable feeling said Lady Maud said Sybil , very gravely exclaimed Lady Maud looking round at her friends said Sybil said Lady Maud looking round to Lord Milford said Mr Mountchesney .
