# text = END OF THE THIRD BOOK BOOK IV enquired Mr Berners at Brookes " of a brother M.P ., about four o'clock in the early part of the spring of 1839 and in a few minutes they left the club said Mr Egerton in an undertone , as if he were afraid a passer-by might overhear him I hope it may ; but I know , in great confidence mind you , that Lord John was saying something about it yesterday said Mr Egerton said Mr Berners said Mr Egerton said Mr Egerton exclaimed Lord Fitz-Heron , who was leaning on the arm of Lord Milford , and who met Mr Egerton and his friend in Pall Mall said Lord Milford said Mr Egerton said Berners said Lord Milford said Mr Egerton said his companion said Lord Fitz-Heron said Lord Milford Egerton and Berners walked on a little further .
