# text = The delegates made their accustomed statement ; they wished to pledge no one ; all that the people desired was a respectful discussion of their claims ; the national petition , signed by nearly a million and a half of the flower of the working classes , was shortly to be presented to the House of Commons , praying the House to take into consideration the five points in which the working classes deemed their best interests involved ; to wit , universal suffrage , vote by ballot , annual parliaments , salaried members , and the abolition of the property qualification said Lord Valentine replied one of the delegates said Lord Valentine said one of the delegates smiling , but in a tone of kindness and respect said Lord Valentine said the other delegate said Lord Valentine said the delegate said Lord Valentine said the delegate said Lord Valentine said the other delegate said the delegate who had chiefly spoken said Lord Valentine smiling said the delegate said the other delegate said Lord Valentine , turning to the delegate and smiling said the delegate said Lord Valentine , as they all rose said the tall delegate said Lord Valentine said the tall delegate said his companion said the tall delegate said the tall delegate to his companion , as they descended the staircase said his friend said the tall delegate laughing said his companion , as he knocked said the tall delegate
