# text = The direction was to said Morley , looking very intently upon the person to whom he spoke -- a portly man and a comely ; florid , gentleman-like , but with as little of the expression which Morley in imagination had associated with that Hatton over whom he once pondered , as can easily be imagined said the strange gentleman and Morley bowed ; and going in different directions , they separated inquired Morley of his friend the journalist , when , having transacted their business , the occasion served was the reply said the journalist said Morley said his friend inquired Morley , evidently much interested , though he attempted to conceal his emotion replied his friend the journalist added laughingly A strong impression was on the mind of Morley that this was his man : he resolved to inquire of Gerard , whom he should see in the evening , as to the fact of their Hatton being a Catholic , and if so , to call on the antiquary on the morrow .
