# text = In the midst of a delightful conversation that seemed to approach a crisis , Lady St Julians was sure to advance , and interfere with some affectionate appeal to Lady Joan , whom she called her " dear child " and while she did not deign even to notice the unhappy cavalier whom she had thus as it were unhorsed said Lady St Julians to Lady Joan Lady Joan looked as if the absence or presence of Frederick was to her a matter of great indifference , and then she added said Lady St Julians said the Duke of Fitz-Aquitaine , who with the viceroyalty of Ireland dexterously dangled before his eyes for the last two years , had become a thorough conservative and had almost as much confidence in Sir Robert as in Lord Stanley said Lady St Julians A foreign diplomatist of distinction had pinned Lord Marney , and was dexterously pumping him as to the probable future said the diplomatist said Lord Marney and here the diplomatist stopped and looked up in Lord Marney's face , as if he would convey something that he would not venture to express said Lord Marney Lord Deloraine and Mr Ormsby passed by ; the diplomatist addressed them said Lord Deloraine said the diplomatist , and he looked up in the face of Lord Deloraine said Lord Deloraine said the diplomatist said Lord Deloraine as he walked away with Mr Ormsby said Mr Ormsby demurely Lady Firebrace and Lady Maud Fitz-Warene were announced : they had just come from the Commons ; a dame and damsel full of political enthusiasm .
