# text = Lord de Mowbray advancing was met accidentally on purpose by Mr Tadpole , who seemed anxious to push forward to Lord Marney said Tadpole in a suppressed tone Tadpole had now succeeded in tackling Lord Marney alone ; the other peers were far out of ear-shot said the honest gentleman in a peculiarly confidential tone , and with a glance that spoke volumes of state secrecy said Lord Marney exclaimed Mr Tadpole said his Lordship said Mr Tadpole mysteriously he added with a sanctimonious air and here he broke into a horse smile
