# text = But with a solemn sweetness , and as it were a tender inflexibility , the tears trickling down her beautiful cheek , and pressing his hand in both of hers , she subdued and put aside all his efforts she said END OF THE FOURTH BOOK BOOK V said Mr Egerton at Brookes' said a grey-headed gentleman , speaking without taking his eyes off the newspaper said Mr Egerton said Mr Berners said Mr Egerton said the grey-headed gentleman said a Warwickshire peer said the grey-headed gentleman said Mr Egerton Here several gentlemen entered , enquiring whether the evening papers were in and what was the news from Birmingham said one of them said the grey - headed gentleman enquired Mr Berners said Mr Egerton said Mr Berners said Mr Egerton said Mr Berners said Mr Egerton said the grey-headed gentleman said the Warwickshire peer said Mr Egerton said Egerton said Mr Berners suggested the Warwickshire noble said the grey-headed gentleman said Mr Egerton enquired Lord Loraine , a mild , middle-aged , lounging , languid man , who passed his life in crossing from Brookes' to Boodle's and from Boodle's to Brookes' , and testing the comparative intelligence of these two celebrated bodies ; himself gifted with no ordinary abilities cultivated with no ordinary care , but the victim of sauntering , his sultana queen , as it was , according to Lord Halifax , of the second Charles Stuart said the grey - headed gentleman said the Warwickshire peer ; pretending that the People can be better off than they are , is radicalism and nothing else said Lord Loraine said Mr Egerton said the Warwickshire peer said Lord Loraine said the grey - headed gentleman said Lord Loraine said Mr Berners
