# text = All this Hatton understood ; it was a conclusion he had gradually arrived at by a gradual process of induction and by a vigilant observation that in its study of character had rarely been deceived ; and when one evening with an art that could not be suspected , he sounded Gerard on the future of his daughter , he found that the clear intellect and straight-forward sagacity of the father had arrived at the same result said Gerard During these two months , and especially during the last , Morley was rarely in London , though ever much with Gerard , and often with his daughter during his visits .
