# text = She hesitated ; it did not agree with the description that had been given her by the coffee-house keeper , but she had seen so much since , and felt so much , and gone through so much , that she had not at the moment that clear command of her memory for which she was otherwise remarkable ; but while she faltered , an inner door was violently thrown open , and Sybil moving aside , two girls , still beautiful in spite of gin and paint , stepped into the Street exclaimed Sybil starting back , overwhelmed with shame and terror exclaimed an Irishman , who was one of the group on the outside said Sybil appealing to the man who had thus spoken and whom she gently drew aside said the man and he looked round , but the young man had disappeared he added said Sybil Nor did Sybil fear ; for the description of the street which the honest man had incidentally given , tallied with her instructions .
