# text = It was generally whispered about that the Liberator at the head of the Hell-cats and all others who chose to accompany them was going to pay a visit to Mr Trafford's settlement , in order to avenge an insult which his envoys had experienced early in the morning when , accompanied by a rabble of two or three hundred persons , they had repaired to the Mowedale works in order to signify the commands of the Liberator that labour should stop , and if necessary to enforce those commands .
