# text = But he had heard Devilsdust for years declare that Stephen Morley was the deepest head in Mowbray , and though he regretted the unfortunate weakness in favour of that imaginary abstraction called Moral Force for which the editor of the Phalanx was distinguished , still Devilsdust used to say that if ever the great revolution were to occur by which the rights of labour were to be recognised , though bolder spirits and brawnier arms might consummate the change , there was only one head among them that would be capable when they had gained their power to guide it for the public weal , and as Devilsdust used to add and that was Morley .
